      "text": "Given that when $n$ is divided by $6$, a remainder of 1 is given, we have:\n\\[ n = 6k + 1 \\]\nfor some integer $k$.\n\nWe are asked to find the remainder when $n + 2010$ is divided by $6$.\n\nFirst, calculate $(n + 2010)$:\n\\[ n + 2010 = (6k + 1) + 2010 = 6k + 2011 \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine what remainder $2011$ leaves when divided by $6$. To do this, we perform the division of $2011$ by $6$:\n\\[ 2011 \\div 6 = 335 \\text{ R } 1 \\]\nThis indicates that:\n\\[ 2011 = 6 \\cdot 335 + 1 \\]\nThus:\n\\[ 2011 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ 6k + 2011 \\equiv 6k + 1 \\pmod{6} \\]\nSince:\n\\[ 6k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{6} \\]\nwe have:\n\\[ 6k + 2011 \\equiv 0 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when $n + 2010$ is divided by $6$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
